WEBVTT

00:00:01.330 --> 00:00:03.610
In 2167...

00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:06.700
...the Earth suffered incredible damage...

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:08.930
...from the supernova of the star.

00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:14.570
But people all over the world have united together to survive.

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:18.270
People of the past, thank you.

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:20.550
The Earth is well.

00:00:21.890 --> 00:00:23.760
And I'm doing good as well somehow.

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:28.300
It's the year is 2356.

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:36.890
Sora wo aogi Hoshi yo michite Tobitatsu no Asu e no brilliant road

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:36.890
Look up to the sky, rise to the stars, Take-off on the brilliant road of tomorrow

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:36.890
空を仰ぎ 星よ満ちて 飛び立つの 明日への brilliant road

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:44.840
Kokoro no aosa Kono te ni daite go far away

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:44.840
Carry the unexpierence of the heart in the hands and go far away

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:44.840
心の蒼さ この手に抱いて go far away

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:59.940
Urayamu koto ni Narete shimattara

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:59.940
If you have experienced the envy

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:59.940
羨む事に 慣れてしまったら

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:05.970
Hokoreru jibun ga Toozakatteku

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:05.970
Your proud self will go far away

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:05.970
誇れる自分が 遠ざかってく

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:13.140
Mienai tsubasa de habataku no fly higher

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:13.140
Flapping the invisible wings to fly higher

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:13.140
見えない翼で羽ばたくの fly higher

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:20.470
Yume wo egaku no wa hito ni umareta kara

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:20.470
I'm imaging dreams because I was born a "person"

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:20.470
夢を描くのは「人」に生まれたから

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:24.580
Sora wo aogi Hoshi yo michite

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:24.580
Look up to the sky, rise to the stars,

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:24.580
空を仰ぎ 星よ満ちて

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:28.040
Tobitatsu no Asu e no brilliant road

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:28.040
Take-off on the brilliant road of tomorrow.

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:28.040
飛び立つの 明日への brilliant road

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:32.920
Kokoro no aosa Kono te ni daite

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:32.920
Carry the unexperienced of the heart in the hands

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:32.920
心の蒼さ この手に抱いて

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:40.850
Anata to nara Yowai jibun wo sarakedashite hashiridaseru no

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:40.850
If I were with you, I'd start running, exposing my weak self

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:40.850
あなたとなら 弱い自分をさらけ出して走り出せるの

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:48.540
Mirai yo dou ka Mugen ni tsuzuke go far away

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:48.540
The future! Somehow continues to the infinity, go far away

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:48.540
未来よどうか 無限に続け go far away

00:02:01.010 --> 00:02:06.680
Episode Eight:
 Me?

00:02:22.210 --> 00:02:23.970
Is that one of the Tatsunoff Generators...

00:02:24.580 --> 00:02:26.450
...which are pivotal to the Great Mission?

00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:29.280
This is humanity's greatest strategy.

00:02:29.550 --> 00:02:31.720
It's gotten lively around here, hasn't it?

00:02:31.810 --> 00:02:34.030
You don't think about what happens if we fail?

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:35.540
We will succeed.

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:36.380
What do you base that on?

00:02:37.010 --> 00:02:39.350
You don't need a basis for something you believe in.

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:40.680
True.

00:03:06.070 --> 00:03:07.350
Wow!

00:03:07.430 --> 00:03:09.090
Shipon's so fast, so fast!

00:03:09.230 --> 00:03:12.060
Yeah. Shipon's really been trying hard recently.

00:03:12.260 --> 00:03:15.380
Just recently, she did the zero-G activity practice by herself.

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:23.480
Last one!

00:03:27.790 --> 00:03:30.220
Two minutes, 20 seconds! The top record for today!

00:03:35.250 --> 00:03:38.450
That was incredible, Shipon! You passed Milady!

00:03:38.750 --> 00:03:39.820
Thanks.

00:03:40.030 --> 00:03:42.450
But I'm still not good enough yet.

00:03:43.410 --> 00:03:45.820
The record Ayaka set when she was a preparatory student...

00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:47.190
...was two minutes and five seconds.

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:52.690
Why you, why you, why you!

00:03:52.860 --> 00:03:55.750
Could it be you're proclaiming her as your rival!?

00:03:53.910 --> 00:03:54.860
Stop it!

00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:59.540
Hey now! This isn't martial arts class!

00:04:00.470 --> 00:04:01.970
S-sorry. 
S-sorry.

00:04:03.960 --> 00:04:05.510
What about the next two?

00:04:11.690 --> 00:04:14.030
It looks like they'll pass four minutes, doesn't it?

00:04:14.790 --> 00:04:18.540
After the best record gets broken, the worst one does, too.

00:04:19.090 --> 00:04:19.630
Huh?

00:04:21.290 --> 00:04:22.590
Who's that?

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:25.000
That's not a spacesuit from the Stellvia, is it?

00:04:30.680 --> 00:04:31.580
What!?
What!?

00:04:32.390 --> 00:04:33.030
Hmm.

00:04:40.260 --> 00:04:41.270
Two minutes, five seconds!

00:04:43.520 --> 00:04:46.090
A tie record? With Ayaka?

00:04:58.040 --> 00:04:59.740
Rinna...?

00:05:00.120 --> 00:05:02.550
Ding ding! Absolutely correct.

00:05:02.710 --> 00:05:03.900
We meet again.

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:11.980
Wow, she's so cute!

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:13.310
Where's she from? Where's she from?

00:05:13.590 --> 00:05:15.300
Her hair is all curly.

00:05:15.420 --> 00:05:17.120
She looks like a doll!

00:05:18.950 --> 00:05:22.300
Uh... things have happened in reverse, but let me introduce her.

00:05:22.730 --> 00:05:23.860
This is our new transfer student...

00:05:23.950 --> 00:05:25.560
I'm Rinna Kazamatsuri.

00:05:25.770 --> 00:05:29.100
I came from the furthest away Foundation, the Ultima.

00:05:29.560 --> 00:05:30.660
Her name's Rinna!

00:05:30.800 --> 00:05:32.170
From the Ultima, she said!

00:05:32.390 --> 00:05:34.140
From so far away, by herself?

00:05:34.470 --> 00:05:37.830
She's twelve years old, but her grades are excellent...

00:05:37.940 --> 00:05:39.620
...so she's been admitted as a preparatory student.

00:05:40.170 --> 00:05:41.370
She's young, but...

00:05:41.930 --> 00:05:45.170
Jojo, her abilities are far greater than yours.

00:05:45.290 --> 00:05:46.130
Really...

00:05:46.590 --> 00:05:47.890
Hey, why me!?

00:05:59.980 --> 00:06:01.160
All right then, let's have...

00:06:01.770 --> 00:06:03.190
Kazamatsuri, you answer this.

00:06:03.620 --> 00:06:04.320
Yes, sir!

00:06:04.740 --> 00:06:06.310
According to the Kerr-Newman equation...

00:06:06.400 --> 00:06:09.740
...as a black hole revolves, it carries an electrical charge.

00:06:35.230 --> 00:06:36.270
Hm...

00:06:36.730 --> 00:06:39.570
So the Ultima still doesn't have a school yet.

00:06:40.840 --> 00:06:42.430
That's why classes are so much fun.

00:06:42.860 --> 00:06:44.130
They would be.

00:06:44.480 --> 00:06:46.940
If I was that good, I'd have fun, too.

00:06:47.170 --> 00:06:48.670
Don't be jealous, don't be jealous.

00:06:48.750 --> 00:06:51.130
You lost to Rinna, too!

00:06:51.350 --> 00:06:54.260
If you're going to say that, then we all lost.

00:06:55.790 --> 00:06:58.390
Geniuses really do exist, don't they?

00:07:01.570 --> 00:07:03.850
A genius... huh?

00:07:09.700 --> 00:07:12.530
I wonder if I can't compare to a genius...

00:07:12.910 --> 00:07:13.770
Hey, Shipon.

00:07:13.890 --> 00:07:14.200
Huh!?

00:07:14.840 --> 00:07:16.610
Do you have any plans after you eat?

00:07:16.750 --> 00:07:18.200
No, I don't.

00:07:18.510 --> 00:07:20.810
Then after you're done, how about a match with me?

00:07:21.030 --> 00:07:22.040
A match!?

00:07:24.980 --> 00:07:26.920
It looks like there will be six members selected...

00:07:27.190 --> 00:07:30.320
...from the regular students for the Great Mission.

00:07:30.520 --> 00:07:32.630
Four of them will be us, and...?

00:07:32.970 --> 00:07:35.290
Maybe Youko Kusanagi, Rin Tamahana...

00:07:35.360 --> 00:07:38.060
...Yuko Nishina, or...?

00:07:38.130 --> 00:07:39.290
Shima Katase.

00:07:41.040 --> 00:07:43.840
That's right. The preparatory students could be candidates, too.

00:07:43.990 --> 00:07:47.570
It couldn't be. Just because she did a bit of work in astroball...

00:07:48.100 --> 00:07:49.080
Care to bet on it?

00:07:49.490 --> 00:07:51.040
It's nothing worth betting on.

00:07:53.010 --> 00:07:54.430
It looks like they've confirmed...

00:07:54.610 --> 00:07:57.080
...an unidentified flying object in the Ultima's surrounding area.

00:07:57.520 --> 00:07:58.190
And thus...

00:07:58.250 --> 00:08:02.010
...Technical Officer Kazamatsuri's daughter has been left with us.

00:08:02.500 --> 00:08:05.880
Seriously, with the Great Mission so close at hand...

00:08:06.520 --> 00:08:07.850
But that's why, isn't it?

00:08:08.400 --> 00:08:10.710
The Ultima, which is going to receive the Second Wave first...

00:08:10.860 --> 00:08:12.130
...is full of press.

00:08:12.530 --> 00:08:14.330
It's the most suitable move against them.

00:08:14.670 --> 00:08:17.060
People who believe the end is coming, and fatalists...

00:08:17.590 --> 00:08:20.700
The human race is in peril, so why can't everyone unify?

00:08:21.060 --> 00:08:23.900
It means that it's difficult to get people to understand each other.

00:08:24.110 --> 00:08:25.490
How's the transfer student?

00:08:26.760 --> 00:08:29.820
She's doing fine. She's the genius girl the rumors say she is.

00:08:30.290 --> 00:08:32.070
Among the preparatory students, she's top of the class.

00:08:32.570 --> 00:08:34.090
Is she good encouragement?

00:08:34.620 --> 00:08:36.650
Some students are feeling just the opposite and getting depressed.

00:08:47.840 --> 00:08:51.630
Rank B. Your grade is rank B.

00:08:55.270 --> 00:08:59.100
Good! Rank A. Your grade is rank A.

00:08:59.490 --> 00:09:03.220
All right, rank A! I win!

00:09:03.740 --> 00:09:05.640
This makes it three wins in a row for me.

00:09:05.880 --> 00:09:07.130
What do you want to do next?

00:09:07.420 --> 00:09:09.880
I just can't compare to you, Rinna.

00:09:10.130 --> 00:09:12.290
How are you so skilled?

00:09:12.480 --> 00:09:12.970
Huh?

00:09:14.850 --> 00:09:18.350
Well, because I do it a lot.

00:09:18.580 --> 00:09:19.360
A lot?

00:09:19.570 --> 00:09:22.080
Yeah, a lot, ever since I was a little kid!

00:09:23.800 --> 00:09:25.830
The amount of time I've lived on the Ultima...

00:09:25.910 --> 00:09:28.640
...is much longer than the amount of time I've lived on Earth.

00:09:29.310 --> 00:09:30.950
I've pretty much been mostly on the Ultima, I guess.

00:09:31.760 --> 00:09:34.770
There aren't many children on the Ultima.

00:09:35.210 --> 00:09:36.970
And the adults are busy, too...

00:09:37.400 --> 00:09:39.860
That's why I played on the simulators so much.

00:09:40.990 --> 00:09:44.780
To me, zero-G activities and using the simulators are an everyday thing.

00:09:45.070 --> 00:09:46.190
Of course I'm going to be good at them.

00:09:46.790 --> 00:09:48.420
I'm kind of a cheater, aren't I?

00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:52.210
Rinna has been doing this since long ago.

00:09:52.960 --> 00:09:57.240
That's right, there's no way she would be this good if she had just started.

00:09:57.760 --> 00:09:59.440
I'm sure that Ayaka also...

00:10:00.110 --> 00:10:02.560
Shipon, have you ever been in a snowball fight?

00:10:02.650 --> 00:10:02.970
What?

00:10:03.720 --> 00:10:07.740
I've never seen snow. On Earth, it falls, right?

00:10:08.140 --> 00:10:10.430
It's not that it falls everywhere, but...

00:10:11.380 --> 00:10:12.680
What about where you live, Shipon?

00:10:12.750 --> 00:10:15.280
It falls, and I've been in snowball fights.

00:10:15.690 --> 00:10:19.050
A snowball fight. I've always wanted to play something like that.

00:10:19.510 --> 00:10:21.210
Then come over and play sometime.

00:10:21.440 --> 00:10:23.290
Let's have a snowball fight together.

00:10:23.640 --> 00:10:24.450
Really!?

00:10:24.710 --> 00:10:27.970
Yeah. I'll teach you lots of other things, too...

00:10:28.030 --> 00:10:30.350
...like making snow houses, skiing, and making snowmen.

00:10:30.670 --> 00:10:31.970
All right!

00:10:31.940 --> 00:10:36.390
In that case, in that case, I'll teach you how to use the Ultima's spaceboards.

00:10:36.580 --> 00:10:38.300
The trick to doing the turns is to turn your hips...

00:10:38.390 --> 00:10:40.940
...with a quick sway, like this, sway!

00:10:41.190 --> 00:10:42.980
Sway?
 Right, sway!

00:10:43.450 --> 00:10:44.910
Sway, sway!

00:10:45.420 --> 00:10:46.980
Sway, sway!

00:10:47.530 --> 00:10:48.800
Sway, sway, sway!

00:10:49.290 --> 00:10:50.650
Sway, sway, sway!

00:10:51.160 --> 00:10:52.120
Sw-sw-sw-sway!

00:10:52.640 --> 00:10:53.760
Sw-sw-sw-sway!

00:10:53.890 --> 00:10:55.020
Sway-sway-sway-sway!

00:10:55.160 --> 00:10:56.490
Sway-sway-sway-sway!

00:11:10.980 --> 00:11:13.810
Because of the Tatsunoff Generator expansion operations...

00:11:14.240 --> 00:11:16.470
...every block but B is off limits.

00:11:16.730 --> 00:11:18.180
Yes, ma'am, I'll be careful.

00:11:21.180 --> 00:11:22.110
All right!

00:11:23.790 --> 00:11:24.480
Hmm?

00:11:26.820 --> 00:11:27.460
Hmm...

00:11:29.480 --> 00:11:31.130
It looks like she's going to do independent practice.

00:11:31.450 --> 00:11:32.430
Forward thinking, isn't she?

00:11:32.930 --> 00:11:34.600
When she looks forward, she only looks forward.

00:11:35.030 --> 00:11:36.800
When she looks back, she only looks back.

00:11:37.200 --> 00:11:38.130
That's true...

00:11:38.480 --> 00:11:41.230
It would be good for that girl to look more to her sides.

00:11:41.600 --> 00:11:43.610
She gains confidence and then loses it...

00:11:44.120 --> 00:11:46.260
It feels like the difference between the two is too large.

00:11:46.860 --> 00:11:47.930
Are you worried?

00:11:48.050 --> 00:11:48.600
Yes.

00:11:48.940 --> 00:11:52.530
Right now, she's going between being full of herself and being depressed.

00:11:52.990 --> 00:11:56.030
In doing that, she will increase her own capabilities.

00:11:56.690 --> 00:11:58.140
They are young, after all.

00:12:10.520 --> 00:12:12.970
There isn't a person that was good right from the start.

00:12:18.300 --> 00:12:21.970
If I can't do it now, then I'd better work hard so I can the next time...

00:12:28.790 --> 00:12:30.120
Next time, I want to...

00:12:33.630 --> 00:12:34.520
...win over Ayaka!

00:12:45.710 --> 00:12:46.840
Oh, Yayoi.

00:12:47.300 --> 00:12:48.430
Do you know where Shipon is?

00:12:48.980 --> 00:12:52.780
I'm sure that she said she was going to practice the Joust...

00:12:53.110 --> 00:12:54.560
I see. Thanks!

00:13:02.710 --> 00:13:03.410
That was shallow...

00:13:03.980 --> 00:13:04.790
One more time.

00:13:13.670 --> 00:13:14.230
What!?

00:13:17.630 --> 00:13:18.210
Who are you?

00:13:19.140 --> 00:13:20.120
It's Rinna!

00:13:20.410 --> 00:13:21.470
Rinna!?

00:13:21.680 --> 00:13:24.840
Practicing with a machine is no fun. Practice with me!

00:13:25.210 --> 00:13:27.740
But if we don't get the teacher's permission...

00:13:27.810 --> 00:13:29.540
We can get it afterwards!

00:13:42.440 --> 00:13:47.200
Rank S! Your grade is rank S!

00:14:02.540 --> 00:14:04.110
Rinna, you're amazing!

00:14:04.180 --> 00:14:06.650
Hey, let's do it Ultima style this time!

00:14:06.720 --> 00:14:07.140
What?

00:14:08.550 --> 00:14:09.280
W-Wait!

00:14:09.600 --> 00:14:11.290
You're not staying on the course!?

00:14:11.360 --> 00:14:14.020
If you can avoid me for ten minutes, then we switch positions.

00:14:18.500 --> 00:14:20.060
Very impressive, Shipon.

00:14:20.130 --> 00:14:21.310
I'm going to be coming after you!

00:14:24.810 --> 00:14:26.690
You were called by Miss Leila?

00:14:27.640 --> 00:14:29.690
So she's gathered the preparatory student dorm leaders, too, then.

00:14:32.610 --> 00:14:33.940
A transfer student has arrived.

00:14:34.010 --> 00:14:34.410
Hm?

00:14:34.910 --> 00:14:36.110
She's skipped a grade.

00:14:36.280 --> 00:14:39.930
Of course, her grades are excellent, and she's very energetic.

00:14:40.420 --> 00:14:42.680
She might be a little bit like you were a long time ago.

00:14:45.390 --> 00:14:47.710
The members who will be chosen for the Great Mission have been decided.

00:14:49.150 --> 00:14:51.150
And regarding that, we thought that we would get you guys...

00:14:51.380 --> 00:14:53.780
...the heads of the dorms, to help with the announcement work.

00:14:54.820 --> 00:14:55.950
Five sheets per person.

00:14:56.090 --> 00:14:56.470
Ugh.

00:14:57.080 --> 00:14:58.550
Posters again?

00:14:58.840 --> 00:14:59.970
It is a tradition, after all.

00:15:07.020 --> 00:15:10.080
A Bianca? But this place is supposed to be off limits...

00:15:12.660 --> 00:15:13.850
All right, let's spread it out.

00:15:14.690 --> 00:15:15.350
Wait a second.

00:15:16.360 --> 00:15:16.830
What!?

00:15:21.220 --> 00:15:22.230
This is nothing!

00:15:24.080 --> 00:15:24.920
Rinna!

00:15:28.430 --> 00:15:30.060
A Bianca in the work area!?

00:15:30.450 --> 00:15:33.050
Yes, one of them is from the Ultima.

00:15:33.540 --> 00:15:34.730
Kazamatsuri!

00:15:41.410 --> 00:15:43.310
Rinna, use your controls.

00:15:43.380 --> 00:15:46.040
At this rate, you'll crash into a generator.

00:15:46.120 --> 00:15:47.850
I am, but...

00:15:49.160 --> 00:15:50.050
She can't be stopped?

00:15:50.400 --> 00:15:52.080
We're not getting a signal on our side.

00:15:52.460 --> 00:15:54.860
The only thing in the area is Shima Katase's Bianca.

00:15:55.170 --> 00:15:56.210
Prepare a rescue craft!

00:15:56.330 --> 00:15:56.790
Yes, ma'am!

00:16:02.970 --> 00:16:04.630
They say it's a Bianca from the Ultima!

00:16:04.700 --> 00:16:05.530
So it's Rinna.

00:16:05.600 --> 00:16:07.160
It looks like she was against Shipon.

00:16:07.240 --> 00:16:08.100
Shipon?

00:16:12.840 --> 00:16:13.470
It's similar...

00:16:14.980 --> 00:16:17.090
Back then, I...

00:16:20.920 --> 00:16:23.800
At this rate, in 40 seconds, she'll collide with it.

00:16:24.200 --> 00:16:27.550
Before that, if I can transfer Rinna over here...

00:16:29.840 --> 00:16:30.420
No...

00:16:30.800 --> 00:16:32.730
If I fail, then Rinna will die.

00:16:33.510 --> 00:16:36.580
If she stays in her Bianca, then at least there's a safety module.

00:16:36.980 --> 00:16:39.100
She might be able to walk away with just minor injuries...

00:16:39.380 --> 00:16:42.110
Shipon, it looks like it's completely hopeless over here.

00:16:42.450 --> 00:16:43.490
Are you planning on getting out!?

00:16:43.690 --> 00:16:46.440
But if I can't get you...

00:16:46.960 --> 00:16:48.810
It's impossible for me...

00:16:48.880 --> 00:16:50.630
It's possible for you, Shipon.

00:16:51.070 --> 00:16:54.810
You're Shima Katase, who did that super shot, and my rival.

00:16:55.170 --> 00:16:55.810
Rival...?

00:16:56.760 --> 00:16:59.690
I came to the Stellvia because you're here, Shipon.

00:16:59.800 --> 00:17:00.200
What?

00:17:00.900 --> 00:17:03.760
I chose the Stellvia because I wanted to challenge you, Shipon.

00:17:04.080 --> 00:17:06.490
I don't have that kind of ability.

00:17:06.910 --> 00:17:09.130
Compared to Ayaka or you, Rinna...

00:17:09.600 --> 00:17:11.570
You don't believe in yourself, Shipon?

00:17:11.830 --> 00:17:12.400
What...?

00:17:12.840 --> 00:17:15.500
If you don't believe in yourself, then believe me.

00:17:15.710 --> 00:17:18.910
In my eyes, that regard you as my rival, Shipon.

00:17:20.300 --> 00:17:23.830
In the teachers that chose you to be an astroball player.

00:17:24.750 --> 00:17:27.670
In the viewers who got completely absorbed by your playing, Shipon.

00:17:30.800 --> 00:17:32.420
Shipon, believe in me.

00:17:32.680 --> 00:17:34.300
I believe in you.

00:17:40.470 --> 00:17:41.860
Is she planning on rescuing her!?

00:17:42.080 --> 00:17:42.990
That's dangerous.

00:17:43.230 --> 00:17:44.680
If it doesn't go well, then the two of them...

00:17:46.700 --> 00:17:48.410
Match up our timing...

00:17:51.420 --> 00:17:53.540
One more time... Calm down...

00:17:57.380 --> 00:17:57.980
She's come out!

00:18:03.120 --> 00:18:04.140
Come to me...

00:18:07.160 --> 00:18:07.980
All right!

00:18:09.920 --> 00:18:12.290
Oh, no! They have too much speed!

00:18:12.360 --> 00:18:13.220
They won't be able to avoid it.

00:18:23.410 --> 00:18:24.520
Hold on...

00:18:33.550 --> 00:18:35.110
There was that method...

00:18:36.350 --> 00:18:37.050
Ayaka...

00:18:37.970 --> 00:18:38.930
Back then...

00:18:42.680 --> 00:18:44.590
No, never mind.

00:19:00.410 --> 00:19:01.160
Um...

00:19:02.250 --> 00:19:03.360
I'm very sorry!

00:19:03.590 --> 00:19:04.170
Sorry!

00:19:07.700 --> 00:19:08.620
Glad you came back.

00:19:10.360 --> 00:19:12.060
I'll be sure to give you your punishment tomorrow...

00:19:12.320 --> 00:19:13.630
...so, for today, rest yourself.

00:19:14.150 --> 00:19:14.640
Ah...

00:19:15.480 --> 00:19:17.100
You did great, Shipon!

00:19:18.740 --> 00:19:19.700
Rinna, you're safe!

00:19:20.330 --> 00:19:22.160
Thank goodness...

00:19:22.360 --> 00:19:22.850
Welcome home.

00:19:23.100 --> 00:19:25.500
Oh, I-I'm home...

00:19:25.570 --> 00:19:26.090
Huh?

00:19:27.910 --> 00:19:28.890
I wonder if it'd be all right.

00:19:29.300 --> 00:19:31.640
I have good news for our hero, Shipon.

00:19:31.900 --> 00:19:32.700
What, what?

00:19:32.780 --> 00:19:36.940
Shipon has been chosen to be a member of the Great Mission.

00:19:37.130 --> 00:19:38.120
Er, wha...?

00:19:38.750 --> 00:19:40.260
You did it!

00:19:40.320 --> 00:19:42.180
Whoa, this is amazing, Shipon.

00:19:42.400 --> 00:19:43.190
It's wonderful.

00:19:43.260 --> 00:19:44.150
Congratulations...

00:19:44.540 --> 00:19:47.620
See, didn't I say that you're amazing, Shipon?

00:19:47.750 --> 00:19:48.670
Really?

00:19:50.000 --> 00:19:53.880
There are six people from the Stellvia. The Big Four, Shipon, and...

00:19:55.570 --> 00:19:57.000
On the bored [Kent Austin - Najima Gebourg - Syoujin Ritsuo - Ayaka Machida - Kouta Otoyama - Shima Katase]

00:19:57.000 --> 00:19:58.590
Kouta Otoyama      Shima Katase

00:19:59.140 --> 00:20:03.040
Kouta Otoyama... why is he one of the chosen members?

00:20:03.130 --> 00:20:04.200
You're not convinced?

00:20:04.460 --> 00:20:06.280
His grades are rank C.

00:20:06.570 --> 00:20:09.710
Among the regular students, there are people with averages of rank A...

00:20:10.040 --> 00:20:12.330
Everything about him is rank C.

00:20:12.590 --> 00:20:17.180
Not his average. Difficult subjects and easy ones, all of them.

00:20:17.440 --> 00:20:19.220
It might just be coincidence.

00:20:19.610 --> 00:20:21.610
Then let me show you something interesting.

00:20:24.800 --> 00:20:25.860
This is...

00:20:25.950 --> 00:20:27.690
This is Kouta Otoyama's vision.

00:20:29.180 --> 00:20:32.510
I'm sure that you understand how amazing this vision is.

00:20:34.560 --> 00:20:41.130
Kouta Otoyama! Congratulations! Rank S. Your grade is rank S.

00:20:41.620 --> 00:20:44.190
Man, that was surprising, that was surprising.

00:20:44.660 --> 00:20:47.750
I can't believe you were chosen to be one of the chosen members...

00:20:47.950 --> 00:20:50.060
But I don't have any self-confidence...

00:20:50.410 --> 00:20:53.040
You're STILL saying that?

00:20:53.210 --> 00:20:54.310
But...

00:20:54.690 --> 00:20:56.920
You'll be able to see the Second Wave from close up.

00:20:57.200 --> 00:20:59.950
It's an honor, so just be honestly happy about it.

00:21:00.500 --> 00:21:01.760
Yes, ma'am...

00:21:03.450 --> 00:21:05.560
If you're a boy, please say your name.

00:21:06.140 --> 00:21:08.190
If you're a girl, then you can come in.

00:21:10.020 --> 00:21:11.170
Rinna?

00:21:13.630 --> 00:21:14.410
What's going on?

00:21:19.470 --> 00:21:19.850
What?

00:21:20.770 --> 00:21:22.990
Thank you, my lifesaver.

00:21:23.260 --> 00:21:24.960
You came all that way to say that?

00:21:26.500 --> 00:21:27.820
You're welcome.

00:21:28.200 --> 00:21:31.290
That, and... nice to meet you, my rival.

00:21:33.090 --> 00:21:34.070
Nice to meet you.

00:21:34.250 --> 00:21:34.940
And...

00:21:35.260 --> 00:21:36.190
There's more?

00:21:36.590 --> 00:21:39.080
Nice to meet you, roommate.

00:21:39.240 --> 00:21:40.900
What... Ah!

00:21:42.310 --> 00:21:43.440
Mwah.

00:21:43.620 --> 00:21:44.310
Whoa!

00:21:46.610 --> 00:21:49.170
What... what...

00:21:49.660 --> 00:21:51.420
What!?

00:21:55.010 --> 00:22:00.540
Atashi wa itsumo sora wo Hikaru sora wo miageteta

00:21:55.010 --> 00:22:00.540
I was always looking up at the sky, the sparkling sky

00:21:55.010 --> 00:22:00.540
あたしはいつも空を 光る空を見上げてた

00:22:01.620 --> 00:22:07.220
Tabitatsu tsubasa te ni ire Kono sora mioroshite mitai no

00:22:01.620 --> 00:22:07.220
I'll obtain wings to take off because I want to look down at this sky

00:22:01.620 --> 00:22:07.220
飛び立つ翼手に入れ この空見下ろしてみたいの

00:22:08.500 --> 00:22:14.980
Mirai wa dou agaitete mo Kanarazu otozureru kara

00:22:08.500 --> 00:22:14.980
Even with how I'm struggling, I'll certainly visit the future

00:22:08.500 --> 00:22:14.980
未来はどうあがいてても 必ず訪れるから

00:22:15.110 --> 00:22:20.890
Dare mo mita koto no nai keshiki wo Nozonde shimau

00:22:15.110 --> 00:22:20.890
I'm wishing for scenery that no one has seen

00:22:15.110 --> 00:22:20.890
誰も見たことのない景色を 望んでしまう

00:22:22.610 --> 00:22:28.670
Todomaru koto wo shiranai Fuan wo kakaeta yume wo

00:22:22.610 --> 00:22:28.670
I don't know about things that stay put, or dreams that hold onto anxiety

00:22:22.610 --> 00:22:28.670
とどまる事を知らない 不安を抱えた夢を

00:22:29.260 --> 00:22:35.590
Ima wa kokoro omomuku mama ni dakou

00:22:29.260 --> 00:22:35.590
Now let's embrace the proceeding spirit

00:22:29.260 --> 00:22:35.590
今は心赴くままに抱こう

00:22:35.940 --> 00:22:42.380
Naite warau tabi ni omou Atashi ga ikiteru imi wo

00:22:35.940 --> 00:22:42.380
I cry every time I think you smile, I'll live for the meaning of it

00:22:35.940 --> 00:22:42.380
泣いて笑う度に思う あたしが生きてる意味を

00:22:42.510 --> 00:22:51.550
Hito wa maru de Irotoridori no hoshi no you da ne

00:22:42.510 --> 00:22:51.550
People are completely multicolored like the stars, you know?

00:22:42.510 --> 00:22:51.550
人はまるで 色とりどりの星のようだね

00:22:52.160 --> 00:22:58.600
Kazaritateta you na kirei na yozora

00:22:52.160 --> 00:22:58.600
The beautifully decked out night sky

00:22:52.160 --> 00:22:58.600
飾り立てたような綺麗な夜空

00:22:58.820 --> 00:23:04.510
Soshite mata Atashi wa miageta

00:22:58.820 --> 00:23:04.510
And still I looked up

00:22:58.820 --> 00:23:04.510
そしてまた あたしは見上げた・・・

00:23:05.020 --> 00:23:07.030
Next episode

00:23:06.090 --> 00:23:06.660
It's Arisa.

00:23:07.160 --> 00:23:08.660
The Great Mission is coming up soon.

00:23:09.270 --> 00:23:12.510
All I, a student, can do is stay in a shelter and pray.

00:23:13.230 --> 00:23:14.130
But I think about them.

00:23:14.630 --> 00:23:16.500
Shipon, who was chosen to be a support member in the Great Mission.

00:23:17.140 --> 00:23:19.790
Rinna, who is separated from her parents on the Ultima.

00:23:20.370 --> 00:23:23.120
I'm always cheerful and lighthearted...

00:23:23.700 --> 00:23:27.770
...but not being of any use at a time like this is a little frustrating.

00:23:28.700 --> 00:23:30.380
On the next episode of Stellvia of the Universe...

00:23:30.640 --> 00:23:31.500
"I'm Going."

00:23:32.050 --> 00:23:35.050
Episode Nine: 
I'm Going "I'm Going."

00:23:32.380 --> 00:23:33.820
Come back safely, Shipon.
